# NOTE: prisma/migrations is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It used to be, and that single line was the root of a serious problem: migrations were never
# shared, so nobody could rebuild the database from them. Drift accumulated invisibly until a fresh
# deploy needed 139 corrective statements to match schema.prisma, which meant production could not
# be recreated from its own history. Migrations ARE the schema's history. They belong in git.

*.log

.vercel

.claude

# Jibri secrets — fill in locally, never commit
scripts/jibri-env.sh

# Local npm overrides — .npmrc is intentionally tracked for Vercel builds
# (Do NOT add .npmrc here)

# Archived pre-baseline migrations (2026-07-13). Kept on disk only; they do NOT reproduce
# schema.prisma, which is why 00000000000000_init replaced them.
prisma/_migrations-archive-*/

# Build artefacts and crash dumps. Neither belongs in history.
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
*.stackdump
